# Cloudflare _redirects. Copied verbatim into dist/ by Vite.
#
# Without these, /resume (no trailing slash) falls through to the SPA-style
# not-found handler and silently serves the homepage instead of the resume —
# verified locally, and this host returns 200 text/html for unknown paths
# rather than a 404, so the failure is invisible.
#
# 302 rather than 301 on purpose: the PDF URL is permanent, but this redirect
# is an alias and a 301 would be cached in browsers effectively forever.
#
# public/resume/index.html stays as a meta-refresh fallback in case this file
# is ever not honoured.

/resume    /kenneth-chen-ko-han-resume.pdf    302
/resume/   /kenneth-chen-ko-han-resume.pdf    302
/cv        /kenneth-chen-ko-han-resume.pdf    302
/cv/       /kenneth-chen-ko-han-resume.pdf    302

# The gated resume needs the passphrase to decrypt the contact details. It is
# a static page (no worker): the phone is only revealed after the browser
# decrypts the AES-256-GCM blob, so it is never served at a guessable URL.
#
# The page lives at public/generate/index.html (a directory, matching the
# /resume pattern) so there is no generate.html file to collide with the
# /generate/ directory - that collision is what made Cloudflare bounce
# /generate.html <-> /generate in a redirect loop. /generate redirects to it;
# /generate/ serves the index directly.
/generate  /generate/   302
